<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DockPops Sparkle appcast — hosted on the PUBLIC release-assets repo
  so anonymous Sparkle clients (running inside installed customer copies
  of DockPops) can fetch updates without GitHub authentication.

  The source code repo (Pixley-Growth/dockpops) is private; only DMGs
  + this appcast + release-notes HTML live here. The split keeps source
  IP private while making distribution fully public.

  Served at: https://pixley-growth.github.io/dockpops-releases/appcast.xml
  Polled by: the Sparkle updater embedded in DockPops Complete
             (configured via SUFeedURL in DockPops/Info.plist).
             Cadence: on launch + every 24h.

  Each <item> represents a shipped version. Sparkle compares the running
  app's CFBundleVersion to <sparkle:version> on each item and offers the
  highest one as an update. The <enclosure>'s sparkle:edSignature is
  verified against the SUPublicEDKey baked into the installed app's
  Info.plist (public key: Fv04mx2fDlTZWiK5uM7dGqJ/PP/Eqphd2XffIfnmVhE=);
  mismatched signatures are silently rejected.

  Per-release update recipe (until the GHA workflow takes over).
  (Shell flags below use a unicode dash so this XML comment stays valid;
   substitute a normal double-hyphen when running the commands.)
    1. Archive + Distribute → Developer ID in Xcode (notarizes + staples)
    2. tools/build-dmg/build-dmg.sh path/to/notarized.app build
    3. codesign –sign "Developer ID Application: Applacat LLC (JN6FKBBBYQ)"
         –timestamp build/DockPops-<version>.dmg
    4. <sparkle>/bin/sign_update –account dockpops-complete
         build/DockPops-<version>.dmg
       → paste sparkle:edSignature + length into a new item below
    5. Push appcast.xml + release-notes/<version>.html to THIS repo
    6. gh release create v<version> build/DockPops-<version>.dmg
         –repo Pixley-Growth/dockpops-releases
-->
